    "result_text": "The build is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented email uniqueness enforcement for the `POST /api/owners` endpoint, following the existing OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (mirroring the telephone-uniqueness rule).\n\n**New files:**\n- `EnsureUniqueEmail.java` \u2014 a pipeline function that rejects a create request whose lower-cased email is already used by any existing owner. It runs after `NormalizeOwnerEmail` (which lower-cases the request email), compares case-insensitively against every stored owner's email, and treats email as optional (a blank request email or a stored owner with no email never collides).\n- `DuplicateEmailException.java` \u2014 a checked exception carrying the offending email.\n- `DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds **409 Conflict** with a `ProblemDetail` body.\n- `officefloor/escalation/\u2026DuplicateEmailException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Wiring change:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted `ensureUniqueEmail` (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) into the pipeline right after `ensureUniqueTelephone`.\n\nThe provided acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` passes, and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
